title: Docker Socket Access for Escape
id: d6e556c2-618d-4cbe-bf87-41558705967c
status: experimental
description: Detects use of the Docker daemon socket (/var/run/docker.sock) via the docker CLI or curl from within a container to launch a privileged container, a common container-escape and host-takeover technique.
author: Alaris Global
references:
  - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1610/
logsource:
  product: linux
  category: process_creation
detection:
  selection:
    CommandLine|contains: '/var/run/docker.sock'
    CommandLine|contains:
      - 'docker run'
      - 'curl'
      - 'containers/create'
  condition: selection
fields:
  - CommandLine
  - User
  - Image
falsepositives:
  - Legitimate Docker-in-Docker tooling
level: high
tags:
  - attack.privilege_escalation
  - attack.t1610
